#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Plugins</title>"
msgstr "<title>Modulen</title>"

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Netscape; Plugins"
msgstr "&Netscape;-Modulen"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid "Currently, &konqueror; supports &Netscape; plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem> Configure "
"Konqueror...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> opens the configuration dialog. "
"Select the <guilabel>Plugins</guilabel> page, where you find two tabs: "
"<guilabel>Global Settings</guilabel> to enable plugins and configure how "
"they are used in &konqueror; and <guilabel>Plugins</guilabel> which shows "
"you the &Netscape; plugins that &kde; has found and allows you to scan for "
"plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information see the <ulink url=\"help:/kcontrol/khtml-plugins/index."
"html\"> Browser Plugins</ulink> help page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "&konqueror; Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; releases several useful plugins that interact with &konqueror; in "
"various ways. These are explained briefly below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"Extensions...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to open a dialog with all installed "
"plugins and select the ones you need. All plugins are accessible in the "
"<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Only plugins appropriate for the current mode (file manager or browser) are "
"listed in the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Browser Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Web Page Translation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This uses the machine translation service provided by <ulink url=\"http://"
"babelfish.yahoo.com/\">Yahoo's BabelFish site</ulink> to translate the "
"current <acronym>HTML</acronym> page to whatever language you want (within "
"reason). It can be launched with <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Translate Web Page</guisubmenu></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have a portion of the text on the page selected, that will be "
"translated instead of the entire &URL;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "Not all languages are available from the Babelfish service."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Machine translation is not a perfect science! Babelfish will at best give "
"you a rough translation, and at worst will give you a very funny read. Don't "
"base important decisions on things you have read from a Babelfish translated "
"page, without confirming that the translation is indeed accurate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may only translate web pages that are accessible on the world wide web. "
"To translate any other text, you should go directly to the Babelfish site "
"itself, where you are able to paste in text for translation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "DOM Tree Viewer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <acronym>DOM</acronym> Tree Viewer allows a developer to view the "
"styles, attributes and elements of a web document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guisubmenu>Show DOM Tree</"
"guisubmenu></menuchoice> opens a new window which displays the document "
"object model (DOM) of the current <acronym>HTML</acronym> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default the display starts at the root node of the document, example: "
"<quote>documentElement</quote>, all other nodes that you will see are "
"children or descendants of the root node."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you wish to manipulate the <acronym>DOM</acronym> tree in any way you "
"will have to use an external script to do so."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Web Page Validator"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This plugin uses the W3C HTML validator to validate the current page, very "
"useful when creating web pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Validate &HTML; (by URI)</guimenuitem> / <guimenuitem>Validate "
"&HTML; (by Upload)</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The validate &HTML; option allows you to compare your &HTML; document to the "
"defined syntax of &HTML; and reports any errors found. Validating your "
"&HTML; will ensure that your pages display properly on all browsers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "Validate CSS (by URI)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to validate your &CSS; style sheet that is embedded in an &HTML; "
"or &XHTML; document. Having valid &CSS; is critical to ensuring that your "
"web site maintains a consistent look regardless of the browser that is being "
"used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "Validate Links"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to confirm that the links on your site contain no redirects or "
"broken links. This tool recursively checks all links on a site."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Validate Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Validates the current page but does not show the result in another window or "
"tab as the previous actions. Using this item enables the action "
"<guimenuitem>View Validator Report</guimenuitem> to display a summary of the "
"validation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Validator"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The configure validator item allows you to view the preset validators you "
"can use to validate your &HTML; and &CSS;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "HTML Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guisubmenu>HTML Settings</"
"guisubmenu></menuchoice> to enable or disable a number of HTML settings "
"without going through the <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "JavaScript"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allows you to turn the use of JavaScript in &konqueror; on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Java"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allows you to turn the use of &Java; in &konqueror; on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cookies"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allows you to turn the use of Cookies in &konqueror; on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenuitem>Plugins</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to turn the use of the &konqueror; plugins you have installed on "
"or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Autoload Images"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allows you to turn on or off the loading of images in web pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable Proxy"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to enable or disable the use of a proxy in the &konqueror; "
"browser."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable Cache"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to enable or disable the use of a cache in the &konqueror; "
"browser."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cache Policy"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Cache Policy submenu provides you with a way to configure how "
"&konqueror; uses a cache. The possible uses include:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keep Cache in Sync"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use Cache if Possible"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "Offline Browsing Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Agent Changer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guisubmenu>Change Browser "
"Identification</guisubmenu></menuchoice> to get a menu that allows you to "
"change the User Agent string without going through the <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu> dialog procedure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The plugin allows you to change the Browser and Operating System "
"identification on a domain-by-domain basis. This is useful when browsing "
"websites that limit access to those using a particular web browser."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default Identification"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default User Agent header for &konqueror; is Mozilla/5.0(compatible;"
"Konqueror/4.7)(KHTML/4.7, like Gecko). If you come across a site that "
"refuses this browser access, change your User Agent to one of the options "
"below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid "Browser submenu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following menu items show a list of popular browsers such as "
"<guimenuitem>Firefox</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Internet Explorer</"
"guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Netscape Navigator</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Opera</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Other</guimenuitem>, and "
"<guimenuitem>Safari</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "Apply To Entire Site"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option allows you to specify that the defined User Agent applies across "
"every page on the site you are visiting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting <guimenuitem>Configure</guimenuitem> opens the settings dialog and "
"allows you to fine tune the amount of information you wish to reveal about "
"the browser and operating system being used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid "Archive Web Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Invoked with <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guisubmenu> Archive Web "
"Page</guisubmenu></menuchoice>, this tool creates an archive (<literal role="
"\"extension\">.war</literal> ) file containing the web page being viewed "
"including the images. <mousebutton>Left</mousebutton> click on the archive "
"file name to view the saved page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Manager Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "Folder View Filter"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is controlled by <menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;"
"&Shift;<keycap>I</keycap></keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Show Filter Bar</guisubmenu></menuchoice> and allows you "
"to choose which types of item are displayed in a folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "Image Gallery"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In File Manager mode, you can select <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Create Image Gallery</guisubmenu></menuchoice> or use "
"<keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>I</keycap></keycombo> to create an HTML page with "
"thumbnails of all the images in the current folder. By default the HTML page "
"is called <filename>images.html</filename> and the thumbnails are put into a "
"new <filename>images</filename> folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start the Image Gallery plugin a dialog opens allowing you to "
"adjust the way the gallery is created."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid "Page Look"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Look dialog is for adjusting the appearance of the gallery page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: plugins.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid "Look Dialog Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: plugins.docbook:327 plugins.docbook:398 plugins.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "Page title"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Page title option has a text input box for changing the title of the "
"image gallery page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "Images per row"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Images per row option has a slider and a spin box for adjusting the "
"number of thumbnails that are in a single row in the gallery."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show image file name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Show image file name check box allows you to choose whether to display "
"filenames below the gallery thumbnails."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show image file size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Show image filesize check box allows you to choose whether to display "
"filesizes below the gallery thumbnails."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show image dimensions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Show image dimensions check box allows you to choose whether to display "
"image dimensions in pixels below the gallery thumbnails."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "Font name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Font name combo box provides you with a choice of which font to use in "
"creating the gallery."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "Font size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Font size spin box is for changing the size of the font you selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Foreground color"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Foreground color option has a selector for choosing the foreground color "
"of the gallery, this includes the text areas."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "Background color"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Background color option has a selector for choosing the background color "
"of the gallery."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "Folders"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Folders dialog is used for choosing where to save the gallery. This "
"dialog is also used to configure which folders are used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: plugins.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "Folders Dialog Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "Save to HTML file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Save to file selector allows you to decide where you want to save your "
"image gallery html page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid "Recurse subfolders"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:413
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Recurse subfolders check box enables recursing of subdirectories. If the "
"check box is enabled, a slider and spin box are enabled to select the "
"recursion depth."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copy original files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Copy original files check box creates an image folder storing copies of "
"the original images used in the gallery."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use comment file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The use comment file check box enables a file selector to choose a comments "
"file to use with your gallery. The comment file contains the subtitles for "
"the images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid "The format of this file is:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: plugins.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# this is a comment, lines starting with '#' are ignored\n"
"FILENAME1:\n"
"Description\n"
"\n"
"FILENAME2:\n"
"Description"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid "Thumbnails"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The thumbnails dialog is used for adjusting the properties of the thumbnails "
"in the gallery."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: plugins.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "Thumbnails Dialog Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid "Image format for the thumbnails"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The image format combo box allows you to choose which format is used for the "
"thumbnail images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid "Thumbnail size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The thumbnail size option provides a slider and spin box for adjusting the "
"size of the thumbnails used in the gallery."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: plugins.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set different color depth"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The set different color depth check box enables a combo box for changing the "
"color depth of the thumbnails if you wish to use a different color depth to "
"that used in the original image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search Bar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Provides a text box for easy access to search engines such as Google. "
"Clicking on the icon on the left side of the search box opens a menu to "
"select and enable different search engines and configure their <ulink url="
"\"help:/kcontrol/ebrowsing/index.html\">Web Shortcuts</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shell Command Plugin"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This plugin enables you to execute a shell command in the current folder and "
"view the output in a separate window."
msgstr ""
